          <h2>The A96 through the Garioch</h2>
          <p>Inverurie sits directly on the A96, the main road connecting Aberdeen to Huntly, Elgin and beyond, and a good number of the breakdowns we attend here happen on that road rather than within the town itself. Traffic on this stretch moves quickly and includes a mix of local commuters and longer-distance journeys, so if you've broken down on the A96 near Inverurie, your direction of travel and the nearest junction help us plan the safest way to reach you.</p>

          <h2>A market town at the centre of a rural area</h2>
          <p>Inverurie itself functions as the main town for a wide surrounding area of smaller villages and farmland in the Garioch. That means some of our call-outs are on quieter rural roads leading into town rather than on the A96 or in the town centre — roads that can be narrower, with fewer passing places and less passing traffic to flag down. If you're on one of these roads, a nearby village name or farm sign is genuinely useful information for us.</p>

          <h2>Rail and road together</h2>
          <p>With a station on the Aberdeen–Inverness line, a number of Inverurie residents combine rail travel with driving — parking at the station or picking someone up from it. A breakdown around the station car park or on the approach roads at peak commuting times can be more disruptive than usual, so let us know if that's your situation and we'll aim to get the vehicle clear as quickly as we can.</p>

          <div class="callout">
            <p><strong>Broken down on a quiet rural road near Inverurie?</strong> These roads can be exposed with little passing traffic. Stay warm, keep your hazards on if it's safe to remain with the car, and give us the nearest village, farm or landmark rather than relying on a postcode alone.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

